## Type-directed auto-call: a bare nullary fn reference auto-calls in a
## non-Fn value position, so `xs` binds the Array result and `xs.len`
## resolves without explicit parens. (The Fn-typed *reference* escape
## hatch is covered by typeck unit tests; calling a first-class named-fn
## value is a separate codegen concern not exercised here.)
def get_items -> Array[Int]
  [10, 20, 30]
end

def main
  let xs = get_items
  let n = xs.len
  puts "#{n}"
end
